1
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:05,591
Alex: Woo! Live from the gap between Lisbon and New York.

2
00:00:05,591 --> 00:00:09,479
Alex: Welcome back to The Office 360 Unfiltered. I am Alex.

3
00:00:09,479 --> 00:00:13,073
Alex: This episode is the anatomy of the studio itself.

4
00:00:13,073 --> 00:00:21,655
Alex: Four senior people, two cities, and how we outbuild a fifty-person agency that needs a meeting to schedule a meeting.

5
00:00:21,655 --> 00:00:27,890
Alex: If you have ever paid for a building and got a hallway, come on. This one is for you.

6
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:33,021
Morgan: Okay, "the anatomy of the studio" sounds very serious for what this actually is,

7
00:00:33,021 --> 00:00:37,712
Morgan: which is four adults in two time zones arguing about a font choice over coffee.

8
00:00:37,712 --> 00:00:43,650
Morgan: But that's the point, isn't it? No floor of account managers, no hallway you're secretly paying for,

9
00:00:43,650 --> 00:00:47,035
Morgan: just the people who actually do the work, doing the work.

10
00:00:47,035 --> 00:00:51,845
Morgan: That fifty-person-agency line got me though. The meeting to schedule the meeting.

11
00:00:51,845 --> 00:00:57,190
Morgan: We have all sat in that meeting. We have all watched it go nowhere for forty-five minutes.

12
00:00:57,570 --> 00:01:03,536
Alex: Woo! We are live, and look at the rundown, no sponsor in the chair today. This hour is ours.

13
00:01:03,536 --> 00:01:06,973
Alex: Welcome back to The Office 360 Unfiltered, I am Alex.

14
00:01:06,973 --> 00:01:12,875
Alex: We told you we hit twenty downloads all over the world. We meant it, we did not inflate it.

15
00:01:12,875 --> 00:01:16,182
Alex: Today is not another roast of a WordPress retainer.

16
00:01:16,182 --> 00:01:20,009
Alex: Today is the growth episode, how you helped this show live.

17
00:01:20,009 --> 00:01:23,770
Alex: Listen, download, subscribe, send a shout out, book an ad.

18
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:29,013
Morgan: Twenty downloads, all over the world, no inflation, no fake dashboard confetti,

19
00:01:29,013 --> 00:01:31,845
Morgan: just real people in real places pressing play.

20
00:01:31,845 --> 00:01:38,001
Morgan: And listen, we know twenty sounds small if you're used to shows that claim numbers nobody can check.

21
00:01:38,001 --> 00:01:42,434
Morgan: We would rather tell you the true twenty than a made-up twenty thousand.

22
00:01:42,434 --> 00:01:47,728
Morgan: And no roast today, which, honestly, feels like a vacation. But don't get comfortable.

23
00:01:47,728 --> 00:01:53,884
Morgan: Because Alex is about to ask you for something, and I want you to actually listen to how he does it.

24
00:01:54,264 --> 00:02:00,290
Morgan: Before Alex gets to the actual ask, let's talk about what "growth episode" has meant so far,

25
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:05,333
Morgan: because it is not us buying followers or running a giveaway for a ring light.

26
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:11,424
Morgan: It's been four people showing up every week, telling true stories about broken donation pages

27
00:02:11,424 --> 00:02:19,087
Morgan: and wedding sites stuck on page 404, and slowly, actually slowly, people started forwarding the show to other people.

28
00:02:19,087 --> 00:02:25,833
Morgan: That is the entire growth strategy. No funnel, no algorithm hack, just "hey, you should hear this one."

29
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:35,198
Morgan: So when Alex asks you for something in a second, know that the twenty of you who are already here are the reason there's an ask to make at all.

30
00:02:35,198 --> 00:02:39,259
Morgan: You built the room. He's just opening the door a little wider.

31
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:49,078
Alex: And if you have a few dollars, and you believe four seniors in Lisbon and New York should keep telling the truth on a microphone,

32
00:02:49,078 --> 00:02:51,200
Alex: there is a donation door too.

33
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:55,883
Alex: I am grinning, because this is the unfiltered version of asking.

34
00:02:55,883 --> 00:03:01,884
Alex: No fake million, no crying violin, just a room that wants a twenty-first listener,

35
00:03:01,884 --> 00:03:07,079
Alex: and a show that wants to stay on the air without selling you a hallway.

36
00:03:07,459 --> 00:03:13,503
Morgan: I love that he will not even let the ask be dramatic. No violin, no fake milestone,

37
00:03:13,503 --> 00:03:19,111
Morgan: just "we exist, we're useful, help us keep existing." That's the whole pitch.

38
00:03:19,111 --> 00:03:25,155
Morgan: So here is exactly how you do that. Story Time is open if you've got a tale for us,

39
00:03:25,155 --> 00:03:30,035
Morgan: email the office techies at gmail dot com, subject line Story Time.

40
00:03:30,035 --> 00:03:37,390
Morgan: Want a Shout Out? Same address, subject Shout Out, tell us what, when, where, and who should show up.

41
00:03:37,390 --> 00:03:45,109
Morgan: Want to Advertise or Donate? Same inbox, subject Advertise or subject Donate, and we will get back to you.

42
00:03:45,109 --> 00:03:53,193
Morgan: Listen, download, subscribe, and tell one person who needs to hear four seniors tell the truth on a microphone.

43
00:03:53,193 --> 00:03:59,019
Morgan: That's it, that's the ask. We'll see you next time on The Office 360 Unfiltered.
